.TH ZFSBACKUPD 1 "October 2026" "zfsbackup" "ZFS Backup"
.SH NAME
zfsbackupd \- ZFS snapshot, retention and remote backup daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zfsbackupd
.RB [ \-c
.IR DATABASE ]
.RB [ \-d ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR LEVEL ]
.RB [ \-\-test\-config ]
.br
.B zfsbackupd \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zfsbackupd
is the supervisor of the zfsbackup worker processes: it creates snapshots of
the configured datasets when they are due, prunes them with the tiered
retention rules, sends them to the configured destinations over HTTPS with
mutual TLS authentication, and, when the server side is configured, receives
other hosts' snapshots.
.PP
It reads its configuration only from the SQLite database managed with
.BR zfsbackup\-config (1);
a YAML file is refused.
It reloads the configuration on SIGHUP and when the database changes, without
interrupting a transfer.
.PP
It is normally started by
.BR systemd (1)
as
.IR zfsbackup.service ,
which is neither enabled nor started by the package.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIDATABASE\fR
The configuration database.
Default: $ZFSBACKUP_CONFIG, else /var/lib/zfsbackup/config.db.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Do not create or destroy snapshots, and create no TLS files.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging; the same as \fB\-\-log\-level debug\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " LEVEL"
One of debug, info (default), warning, error.
.TP
.B \-\-test\-config
Read and validate the configuration, report it, and exit.
It works beside a running daemon.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version, the wire protocol and the configuration schema, and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ZFSBACKUP_CONFIG
The default configuration database.
.TP
.BR ZFS_CMD ", " ZPOOL_CMD
Paths of the \fBzfs\fR and \fBzpool\fR binaries to use instead of those on PATH.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/zfsbackup/config.db
The configuration database, with the host identity and the trust tables.
.TP
.I /var/lib/zfsbackup/config.db.tls/
The TLS identity: certificates and keys.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zfsbackup\-config (1),
.BR zfs (8),
.I /usr/share/doc/zfsbackup/README.md
